# File: scripts/__tests__/nmg-sdlc-smoke.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/605-save-full-smoke-session-transcripts-and-fail-surfaces-whose-transcript-lacks-the-sent-command/requirements.md
Feature: Save full smoke session transcripts and fail surfaces whose transcript lacks the sent command

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Saved transcripts cover the whole session
    Given the smoke instructions in "steering/snippets/project-smoke.md"
    When a surface transcript is saved as instructed
    Then the log is emptied before the surface's command is sent
    And a capture is appended after the command is typed and before Enter is sent
    And the pane is appended to the log at every poll and when the command finishes
    And no instruction overwrites the log with a single final capture

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A transcript without the sent command fails the surface
    Given a passed, head-bound "steering" surface record whose transcript does not contain "/sdlc-steering"
    When the smoke validation checks the record
    Then the validation fails with "nmg-sdlc-smoke surface not exercised: steering"
    And its evidence reads "steering: transcript lacks the sent command"

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Complete transcripts still pass
    Given a passed, head-bound "draft-issue" surface record with command "/sdlc-draft-issue add a thing"
    And its transcript holds that command wrapped across two lines
    When the smoke validation checks the record
    Then the surface passes
    And its evidence names the transcript
